# What a Mac's Brewfile becomes on Linux (lib/core/crossos.sh).
# kind|brew name|apt|dnf|pacman|flatpak
#   A formula not listed here keeps its name, when this system's repositories have it.
#   A cask needs a line: its native package, or else its Flathub id.
#   "-" in a column: nothing to install there (the system has it, or it is a library).
#   "@tool": that dudu collector installs it (nvm, rustup, bun).
#   Empty: no native package; a cask then falls back to its flatpak.
